WEBVTT

1
00:00:06.645 --> 00:00:11.609
upon a time, there was a man who had three sons named Peter, Paul, and Boots.

2
00:00:13.210 --> 00:00:14.491
The father was very poor.

3
00:00:15.232 --> 00:00:17.794
He didn't have a single penny to give to his sons.

4
00:00:18.915 --> 00:00:22.718
One day he said to his sons, "I am poor.

5
00:00:23.578 --> 00:00:25.440
I have nothing to give you.

6
00:00:26.401 --> 00:00:30.304
It is time for you to lead your own lives in the world."

7
00:00:32.668 --> 00:00:37.209
As the brothers were preparing to start their new lives, a man came to their town.

8
00:00:38.790 --> 00:00:43.912
He said to everyone, "Our great king has two terrible tasks.

9
00:00:44.512 --> 00:00:49.153
First, you must chop down a giant oak tree that is blocking his window.

10
00:00:49.773 --> 00:00:51.774
Next, you must dig him a well.

11
00:00:52.474 --> 00:00:57.756
If you complete these two tasks, he will give you half of his kingdom and half of his

12
00:00:57.816 --> 00:01:05.442
treasure. If you fail these tasks, you will be sent to a faraway island."

13
00:01:06.723 --> 00:01:07.804
The father was delighted.

14
00:01:08.764 --> 00:01:10.425
The tasks did not seem too hard.

15
00:01:11.986 --> 00:01:17.149
The brothers were delighted because they had already chopped down many trees and dug a well for their

16
00:01:17.169 --> 00:01:22.192
father. They set off for the palace with dreams of gold and jewels.

17
00:01:23.773 --> 00:01:28.556
What the king's messenger had not said was that as soon as one chip of the oak's trunk

18
00:01:28.616 --> 00:01:31.089
flew off, two more grew back in its place.

19
00:01:33.050 --> 00:01:38.312
The king's messenger also forgot to say that the king's palace was on top of a high hill,

20
00:01:38.692 --> 00:01:40.713
and that this hill was made of solid rock.

21
00:01:42.654 --> 00:01:47.476
When the brothers entered the forest, they heard something chopping and hacking away among the trees.

22
00:01:47.496 --> 00:01:50.878
"Do you hear that sound?"

23
00:01:51.438 --> 00:01:51.999
asked Boots.

24
00:01:52.019 --> 00:01:54.740
"Yes," said Peter and Paul together.

25
00:01:56.240 --> 00:01:59.321
"Is it unusual for a woodcutter to chop trees?"

26
00:01:59.721 --> 00:02:00.321
asked Paul.

27
00:02:00.341 --> 00:02:04.742
"No, but this sounds strange," said Boots.

28
00:02:05.563 --> 00:02:07.143
"I want to see what it is."

29
00:02:07.163 --> 00:02:10.724
"Oh, Boots!

30
00:02:11.344 --> 00:02:12.885
You're the one who is strange.

31
00:02:13.465 --> 00:02:18.346
Our father was too poor to give you a real name, so he named you after an old

32
00:02:18.426 --> 00:02:19.306
pair of boots."

33
00:02:19.947 --> 00:02:21.047
His brothers laughed.

34
00:02:22.787 --> 00:02:24.528
Boots didn't care what they said.

35
00:02:25.344 --> 00:02:29.947
He walked towards the noise, and when he reached where it was coming from, he couldn't believe what

36
00:02:29.987 --> 00:02:30.488
he saw.

37
00:02:31.148 --> 00:02:34.490
There hung an ax, hacking and chopping all by itself.

38
00:02:37.733 --> 00:02:38.333
"Good day!"

39
00:02:38.773 --> 00:02:39.394
said Boots.

40
00:02:39.894 --> 00:02:40.895
"You look busy.

41
00:02:41.455 --> 00:02:42.276
Can I help you?"

42
00:02:42.296 --> 00:02:44.457
"Yes, I am busy.

43
00:02:44.978 --> 00:02:46.819
And, yes, you can help.

44
00:02:47.640 --> 00:02:55.028
I've stood here chopping and hacking for a long time waiting for you," said the ax.

45
00:02:55.048 --> 00:02:58.729
"Well, I'm here, and you can come with us," said Boots.

46
00:02:59.409 --> 00:03:01.610
He took the ax and tucked it under his belt.

47
00:03:05.631 --> 00:03:08.132
From the forest the brothers walked into the mountains.

48
00:03:09.152 --> 00:03:13.594
The mountains were very rocky, but soon they heard a noise that sounded like digging.

49
00:03:13.614 --> 00:03:21.356
"I wonder," said Boots, "what could be digging and shoveling in all this rock?"

50
00:03:24.276 --> 00:03:26.818
"There you go acting strange again.

51
00:03:27.398 --> 00:03:28.338
Poor Boots."

52
00:03:28.539 --> 00:03:29.299
Peter laughed.

53
00:03:30.800 --> 00:03:33.521
"It's just a woodpecker," continued Paul.

54
00:03:33.541 --> 00:03:36.303
"This sounds different," said Boots.

55
00:03:36.323 --> 00:03:39.125
"I think I'll go see what it is."

56
00:03:39.865 --> 00:03:41.026
He climbed up the rocks.

57
00:03:42.026 --> 00:03:43.807
His brothers laughed and made fun of him.

58
00:03:45.628 --> 00:03:47.529
But he didn't let their teasing upset him.

59
00:03:48.890 --> 00:03:51.792
When he got to the top, he couldn't believe what he saw.

60
00:03:53.028 --> 00:03:55.929
There was a shovel that stood digging all by itself.

61
00:03:55.949 --> 00:03:57.989
"Good day!"

62
00:03:58.289 --> 00:03:58.910
said Boots.

63
00:03:58.930 --> 00:04:00.530
"You look busy.

64
00:04:00.870 --> 00:04:01.730
Can I help you?"

65
00:04:02.491 --> 00:04:08.712
"Yes, I am busy," said the shovel, "and yes, you can help.

66
00:04:09.413 --> 00:04:14.254
I've stood here digging and shoveling for a long time waiting for you."

67
00:04:18.095 --> 00:04:21.536
I'm here, and you can come with us," said Boots.

68
00:04:22.444 --> 00:04:24.586
He took the shovel and put it over his shoulder.

69
00:04:26.107 --> 00:04:30.551
After climbing over the mountains, the brothers were thirsty, so they stopped at a brook.

70
00:04:30.571 --> 00:04:35.835
"I wonder where all this water comes from," said Boots.

71
00:04:35.855 --> 00:04:39.418
"We wonder if you're sick in the head."

72
00:04:40.118 --> 00:04:41.379
Peter and Paul laughed.

73
00:04:43.401 --> 00:04:47.224
"Still I would like to see it for myself," said Boots.

74
00:04:47.704 --> 00:04:52.148
"You're crazy, or you'll go crazy soon," said Paul.

75
00:04:52.852 --> 00:04:55.574
"The brook's here; that's all that matters.

76
00:04:55.875 --> 00:04:57.976
Who cares where it comes from?"

77
00:04:59.077 --> 00:05:03.080
"Still I'd like to see it just the same," said Boots.

78
00:05:04.081 --> 00:05:05.082
So he went away.

79
00:05:06.303 --> 00:05:10.166
He followed the brook and soon he could no longer hear the laughter of his brothers.

80
00:05:12.288 --> 00:05:16.371
The brook got smaller and smaller, and finally he couldn't believe what he saw.

81
00:05:19.174 --> 00:05:23.321
There was a large walnut, and out of that walnut came a stream of water.

82
00:05:23.341 --> 00:05:25.102
"Good day!"

83
00:05:25.863 --> 00:05:26.464
said Boots.

84
00:05:27.124 --> 00:05:27.965
"You look busy.

85
00:05:28.485 --> 00:05:29.146
Can I help?"

86
00:05:29.966 --> 00:05:32.268
"Yes, I am," said the walnut.

87
00:05:32.288 --> 00:05:39.354
"And yes, you can, because I have let this water run for a long time waiting for you."

88
00:05:39.374 --> 00:05:43.538
"Well, I'm here," said Boots.

89
00:05:44.118 --> 00:05:48.001
He plugged the hole with some moss, so the water wouldn't run out anymore.

90
00:05:49.302 --> 00:05:51.204
Then he stuffed the walnut into his pocket.

91
00:05:52.640 --> 00:05:54.221
His brothers hadn't waited for him.

92
00:05:55.562 --> 00:06:00.526
They decided that they didn't want to share the kingdom and the treasure with their strange brother, Boots.

93
00:06:04.188 --> 00:06:09.151
The oak was now twice as wide and twice as tall as it had been at first because

94
00:06:09.211 --> 00:06:11.633
two chips grew for every one chopped out.

95
00:06:13.695 --> 00:06:17.978
When Boots reached the city, his two brothers had already tried and failed.

96
00:06:20.179 --> 00:06:23.629
The king was very angry; he had seen many men try and fail.

97
00:06:24.790 --> 00:06:30.593
He looked at Boots and said, "If you are going to perform as well as your brothers, then

98
00:06:30.633 --> 00:06:32.014
go directly to the ship.

99
00:06:34.175 --> 00:06:36.576
I don't want to watch another person fail."

100
00:06:36.596 --> 00:06:41.098
"Well, I can't succeed unless I try," said Boots.

101
00:06:41.999 --> 00:06:46.501
The king wasn't happy, but he gave Boots permission, and Boots took out his ax.

102
00:06:46.521 --> 00:06:48.742
"Chop away!"

103
00:06:49.063 --> 00:06:51.244
he said to the ax, and away it chopped.

104
00:06:52.488 --> 00:06:57.572
It chopped out four chips for every two that grew back, so it wasn't long before the old

105
00:06:57.812 --> 00:06:58.612
oak came down.

106
00:07:01.855 --> 00:07:04.096
When that was done, Boots took out his shovel.

107
00:07:04.116 --> 00:07:05.597
"Dig away!"

108
00:07:06.158 --> 00:07:07.098
he said to the shovel.

109
00:07:07.879 --> 00:07:09.840
And the shovel began to dig and dig.

110
00:07:12.202 --> 00:07:14.163
The rocks flew like leaves in the wind.

111
00:07:15.264 --> 00:07:18.366
Soon he had dug the well, but still there was no water.

112
00:07:19.187 --> 00:07:23.845
Boots took out the walnut, he placed it in one corner of the well, and then he pulled

113
00:07:23.905 --> 00:07:24.525
out the moss.

114
00:07:25.846 --> 00:07:26.646
"Run away!"

115
00:07:27.206 --> 00:07:27.786
said Boots.

116
00:07:29.106 --> 00:07:30.487
And so the water ran out.

117
00:07:31.967 --> 00:07:36.849
At first the well filled with water very slowly, but soon the well filled and made a stream.

118
00:07:38.309 --> 00:07:40.550
The king had all the water he could ever want.

119
00:07:42.030 --> 00:07:46.992
The king gave Boots half his kingdom and half his treasure as promised, but he was so pleased

120
00:07:47.012 --> 00:07:51.626
with Boots, he said, "Is there anything else that I can give you?"

121
00:07:53.207 --> 00:07:59.252
Boots thought for a second and said, "Well, it would be nice if you'd let all the people

122
00:07:59.292 --> 00:08:01.034
who failed come back from the island."

123
00:08:02.315 --> 00:08:07.519
The king agreed and said, "Still that is a gift to those who failed.

124
00:08:07.980 --> 00:08:10.121
Is there anything else I can give to you?"

125
00:08:11.923 --> 00:08:19.221
Boots remembered that his brothers made fun of his name, and he said, "Yes, I would like to

126
00:08:19.281 --> 00:08:20.062
change my name.

127
00:08:20.882 --> 00:08:22.083
Can I be called Mr.

128
00:08:22.123 --> 00:08:26.708
Boots?" The king smiled and said, "Yes, Mr.

129
00:08:26.788 --> 00:08:28.109
Boots, you can."
